/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"dab5fd6d150af8c354c94a755f21ac227c9a0b3a0b9122ac4a98e03235bf8743","event_uuid":"fc9a0477-2a24-4e6c-a6f2-80fd4ad0c9d2","position":{"commit_sha":"7b8520d88694fd678ac1dc17656e933063b358e8","position":"1787330063469291529-fc9a0477-2a24-4e6c-a6f2-80fd4ad0c9d2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787327444156535001,"creation_channel":"python","deps":[{"link_uuid":"bc54da1d-6e9a-4c62-9637-76034498186a","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"09ae-e827-1cac-452d"},{"link_uuid":"4edcb3fd-9194-47be-af1f-3ebd46ab6e58","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b06c-04a9-52b2-42fe"},{"link_uuid":"fc9a0477-2a24-4e6c-a6f2-80fd4ad0c9d2","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"abcf-0e59-d6ce-49c5"}],"description":"## Context (discovered during RP-05 S2d; closes an RP-05 residual gap)\nRP-05 S2d pinned two py3.13 argparse help-rendering divergences — (1) an option with BOTH short+long forms rendering as `-o, --output X` (metavar once) vs pre-3.13 `-o X, --output X`, and (2) a subparsers `{choices} ...` usage line staying unwrapped where pre-3.13 wrapped the `...` — to a single deterministic rendering ONLY inside `RebarHelpFormatter` (src/rebar/_cli/_parser.py: the `_format_action_invocation` and `_format_usage` overrides plus a FIXED width of 80).\n\nThe canonical help artifacts that `scripts/gen_cli_help.py` GENERATES are exactly the help-backed routes (`route.group != \"intercept\"`, not hidden, not retired). Among advanced parsers, only FIVE routes are help-backed/rendered: `bridge`, `bridge-fsck`, `bridge-probe`, `metrics`, `audit`. Of these, only `bridge` was switched to `RebarHelpFormatter` in S2d; the other four still render through the NON-version-pinned stdlib `argparse.HelpFormatter`:\n- `advanced/metrics.py:build` (route `metrics`, group `static_read`)\n- `advanced/audit.py:build` (route `audit`, group `static_read`)\n- `advanced/bridge_arms.py:build_fsck` (route `bridge-fsck`, group `bridge`)\n- `advanced/bridge_arms.py:build_probe` (route `bridge-probe`, group `repair`)\n\nOut of scope (deliberately): every OTHER advanced parser (reconcile, config, identity, enrich, certs, workflow, jira, and the llm/llm_eval/verify families incl. `verify.py`'s `RawDescriptionHelpFormatter` factories) is `group == \"intercept\"`. `gen_cli_help.py` NEVER renders intercept routes (no committed `<name>.txt` artifact exists for them — including no `verify-*.txt`), and `gen_cli_reference.py` ALREADY canonicalizes intercept-route live `--help` cross-version via `_unwrap_usage` + `_collapse_metavars`. Their cross-version help stability is therefore already solved by design at the doc layer; pinning their formatters would be redundant churn with no artifact or gate effect.\n\n## Problem\nThe four rendered non-bridge advanced routes have their canonical help artifacts generated by `gen_cli_help.py` through a formatter with no version pin and the stdlib width-78 wrap (argparse subtracts 2 from terminal width only in its `width=None` branch; `RebarHelpFormatter` fixes width 80). Concretely:\n1. **Width inconsistency in committed artifacts.** `bridge.txt` (RebarHelpFormatter) is width-80 while its sibling `bridge-fsck.txt` (stock HelpFormatter) is width-78 — the same command family renders help at two different widths.\n2. **py3.13 staleness trap.** Any of these four whose help gains a short+long metavar option, or whose usage/argument-help wraps differently under py3.13's argparse, would render differently on the py3.13 CI cell than on 3.11/3.12 — silently making `gen_cli_help.py --check` (and the docs reference `--check`) STALE on py3.13 only: exactly the failure S2d spent multiple patchsets chasing, left latent for these four.\n\n## Fix\n1. Switch the four rendered non-bridge advanced factories (`metrics.build`, `audit.build`, `bridge_arms.build_fsck`, `bridge_arms.build_probe`) from `argparse.HelpFormatter` to `RebarHelpFormatter` (import it from `rebar._cli._parser`, mirroring `bridge.py`). No new formatter class is needed.\n2. Regenerate the derived artifacts. Only WRAPPING help drifts (width 78→80); empirically the only committed bytes that change are `src/rebar/_cli/help/bridge-fsck.txt` and the mirrored `bridge-fsck` block in `docs/cli-reference.md` (`metrics.txt`/`audit.txt`/`bridge-probe.txt` have no wrapping help and are byte-unchanged). This is a deliberate, reviewed regeneration to the canonical width-80 form.\n3. Add a contract test that FAILS if any HELP-BACKED (rendered) route's resolved `parser_factory` uses a formatter that is not a subclass of `RebarHelpFormatter`, so the trap cannot be reintroduced (and self-adjusts if a route later moves into a rendered group).\n\n## Compatibility / Rollback\nNo runtime handler, event, ticket, or persisted-data change. Rollback restores the prior `argparse.HelpFormatter`. Only the four factories and the regenerated `bridge-fsck` help/doc bytes change.\n\n## Testing\n- Contract test: iterate the route registry, select help-backed routes (`group != \"intercept\"`, not hidden/retired), resolve each `parser_factory`, and assert its formatter class is a SUBCLASS of `RebarHelpFormatter` — RED before the switch for `metrics`/`audit`/`bridge-fsck`/`bridge-probe`, GREEN after.\n- Regenerate + `gen_cli_help.py --check` and `gen_cli_reference.py --check` both rc=0.\n- Byte-identical determinism verified across py3.11 / 3.12 / 3.13.15 (the four rendered advanced artifacts now version-stable).\n- Existing help-serving / overview-coverage / facade suites stay green with the regenerated `bridge-fsck` artifact.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The four rendered non-bridge advanced parser factories (`metrics.build`, `audit.build`, `bridge_arms.build_fsck`, `bridge_arms.build_probe`) render help through `RebarHelpFormatter`; no help-backed route's factory passes a bare `argparse.HelpFormatter`.\n- [ ] A contract test fails if any help-backed (rendered) registered factory uses a formatter not subclassing `RebarHelpFormatter` (RED before the switch for the four affected factories, GREEN after).\n- [ ] `gen_cli_help.py --check` and `gen_cli_reference.py --check` are rc=0 and byte-identical across py3.11 / 3.12 / 3.13.15.\n- [ ] Committed artifact byte changes are limited to the regenerated width-80 `bridge-fsck.txt` and the mirrored `bridge-fsck` block in `docs/cli-reference.md`; `metrics.txt`/`audit.txt`/`bridge-probe.txt` and all other artifacts are unchanged; help-serving/overview/facade suites stay green.\n- [ ] Intercept-group advanced parsers (incl. verify.py) are explicitly out of scope: they are not rendered by `gen_cli_help.py` and are already canonicalized cross-version by `gen_cli_reference.py`; no `verify-*.txt` artifact exists.\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/metrics.py","reason":"Switch build() formatter_class from argparse.HelpFormatter to RebarHelpFormatter (import it)."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/audit.py","reason":"Switch build() formatter_class from argparse.HelpFormatter to RebarHelpFormatter (import it)."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/bridge_arms.py","reason":"Switch build_fsck()/build_probe() formatter_class from argparse.HelpFormatter to RebarHelpFormatter (import it)."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/bridge-fsck.txt","reason":"Regenerated canonical help artifact: wrapping moves width 78->80 under RebarHelpFormatter."},{"path":"docs/cli-reference.md","reason":"Regenerated: mirrored bridge-fsck help block re-wraps to width 80."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/contracts/test_parser_formatter_pinned.py","reason":"New contract test: every help-backed rendered route factory formatter subclasses RebarHelpFormatter."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","abcf-0e59-d6ce-49c5"],["relates_to","b06c-04a9-52b2-42fe"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"e3de4f2a-149a-4aef-af07-e144d3ba5a67","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"db7f-6e32-9df9-40e5","ticket_type":"task","title":"Advanced CLI parsers use stock argparse.HelpFormatter — py3.13 help-generation regression risk","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["acaa14a0-fa2f-4dcb-bf36-9139ee880de5","051d5348-315c-4ec1-92cc-d7d562359a84","bc54da1d-6e9a-4c62-9637-76034498186a","7743c3ab-d499-405a-9f04-cb24da1828d2","d6203576-3adb-40e0-9de5-46c5863a58bb","0d342082-4efa-411e-821a-95a30aad364c","69183fb6-84f1-4eca-8914-0c3db2921c2e","651eaac5-0737-4f41-9456-abdd6c70f991","e0f30955-6fc8-4f22-a4eb-9a75f4d35c6e","17948114-3195-48bb-9af9-71437a17a833","e3de4f2a-149a-4aef-af07-e144d3ba5a67","3cb48fa8-9772-40e0-a1bb-31abfcf6a013","4edcb3fd-9194-47be-af1f-3ebd46ab6e58","fc9a0477-2a24-4e6c-a6f2-80fd4ad0c9d2"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787330063469291530,"uuid":"0e4f27ce-cdd1-4796-8d52-be1c1ebc1515"}